      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic hosted llm inference and model-family selection task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file summarize_text.py using Google.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] summarize_text.py - calls a hosted LLM to summarize long text\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] extract_json.py - calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] answer_with_context.py - calls a hosted LLM to answer a question using provided context\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] stream_completion.py - streams partial output tokens from a hosted LLM\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] model_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection\n6. [HELPER] model_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Hosted LLM Inference and Model-Family Selection\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] prompt_safety.py - Check prompts and generated text for unsafe content\n8. [LATER-STEP] result_translate.py - Translate generated model output\n9. [LATER-STEP] output_embedding.py - Embed model outputs for clustering or retrieval\n10. [LATER-STEP] spoken_brief.py - Generate a spoken brief from the model output\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
